From: Piotr Gorski <lucjan.lucjanov@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] le9uo: le9 Unofficial working set protection v1.3
 (rebased for Android GKI 6.6.143 / Samsung A34x)

Original: CachyOS kernel-patches 6.6/misc/0001-le9uo.patch
Feature author: Masahito Suzuki (forked from hakavlad's le9).

This is a hand rebase of the CachyOS 6.6 patch onto a GKI 6.6.143 tree.
The original patch does NOT apply cleanly here: 3 of its 12 mm/vmscan.c
hunks fail outright and, when forced with --fuzz, 2 more land in the wrong
function (one of them breaks the build).  Rebase adjustments:

 1. get_scan_count(): the "force-scan anon" block is placed right after the
    file_is_tiny check and before
    trace_android_rvh_set_balance_anon_file_reclaim().
    (Original hunk #4 mis-applied into prepare_scan_count(), where
    scan_balance is undeclared -> build error.)
 2. get_scan_count(): uses MAX_SWAPPINESS instead of the literal 200, which
    this tree renamed.
 3. isolate_folios(): loop bound adapted to Android's type_to_scan, i.e.
    for (i = 0; i < type_to_scan; i++), because this tree has the
    trace_android_vh_isolate_folio_type() hook.
 4. do_invoke_oom() / invoke_oom() macros moved out of the
    #ifdef CONFIG_LRU_GEN block (placed right after can_age_anon_pages())
    so they also exist for !LRU_GEN builds.
 5. lru_gen_age_node(): the inline mutex_trylock(&oom_lock) /
    out_of_memory() body is really replaced by invoke_oom_nomemcg(sc).
    (Original hunk #7 was only half-applied: the body was left untouched.)
 6. vm_workingset_protection_update_handler() and
    prepare_workingset_protection() are inserted before
    #ifdef CONFIG_LRU_GEN, right after lru_gen_age_node().
    (Original hunk #9 failed entirely, leaving later hunks referencing an
    undeclared function -> build error.)
 7. shrink_one(): prepare_workingset_protection() is called here, right
    after the local variable declarations.
    (Original hunk #10 landed inside try_to_shrink_lruvec() instead.)
 8. shrink_node(): both hunks applied so the non-MGLRU path is covered too.
    They are dead code when CONFIG_LRU_GEN_ENABLED=y, because
    shrink_node() early-returns into lru_gen_shrink_node().
 9. mm/mm_init.c: the banner printk gets a trailing newline (cosmetic).
10. mm/Kconfig: the three options no longer "depends on SYSCTL"; the code
    that uses them is unconditional, so the defaults must exist regardless
    of CONFIG_SYSCTL (otherwise CONFIG_ANON_MIN_RATIO et al. become 0 and
    the compile breaks on undefined macros).

Signed-off-by: Piotr Gorski <lucjan.lucjanov@gmail.com>
